# Boot receipt for the PUBLISHED launcher recipes/kimi-k3/vllm/launch-k3-dspark.sh (and hook/k3ds_guard.py, bench/*.py of this repository,
# exactly as in the tree; no kit-only files), Kimi K3 (vellum-ai/Kimi-K3-W3A16-g64 @09c06868) + Inferact/Kimi-K3-DSpark @ cf6b8244, two Stations,
# vLLM nightly af7f9488, launcher defaults except the rail addresses, model/drafter paths and log dir. One boot, one attempt.
# Excerpt: lines selected verbatim from the raw files named below; hostnames, IPs, user names, GPU UUIDs and private paths replaced with <placeholders>.
# Times are Pacific (PT) unless the line says otherwise; vLLM server log lines are UTC.
# Checks: bench/ksmoke.py (3 canaries, GSM8K first 20 rows, 5 tool calls); real-text C1 x3 (bench/kbench_chat_ds.py, CNN/DailyMail slices from
# bench/build_pool_k3.py); random-id C1 x1 (recipes/nemotron-ultra/bench/bench-nemotron-ultra.sh, CONCS=1 REPS=1).


# NOTE ON THE RANDOM-ID ROW (added by us): recipes/nemotron-ultra/bench/bench-nemotron-ultra.sh passes no --temperature, so vllm bench serve uses the
# server's default sampling (the dump below shows temperature=None). Random-token prompts then produce random continuations that the drafter cannot predict
# (mean accepted length 1.02), the acceptance-gated K turns drafting off (stats-r0.kctl.json: on=false, ema 1.0), and C1 equals the no-drafter speed.
# The 27.6 tok/s random-id figure in logs/kimi-k3/vllm-two-stations-dspark.log was measured with --temperature 0 (greedy), which falls into repetitive output.

